From: Mootjelh <134108676+Mootjelh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:47:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 10211: x86: show both operands of FMUL and FMULP

FMUL ST(0),ST(i) and FMUL ST(i),ST(0) both printed as FMUL STi, and
FMULP ST(i),ST(0) as FMULP STi. Display them the way FADD, FSUB and
FDIV already do. The p-code is unchanged.

Fixes #10204
---
 Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/ia.sinc | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/ia.sinc b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/ia.sinc
index 33b2a6fdf4..a6dff6a451 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/ia.sinc
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/ia.sinc
@@ -7742,19 +7742,19 @@ define pcodeop fldenv;
     FPUInstructionPointer = inst_start;
 }  
 
-:FMUL freg      is vexMode=0 & byte=0xD8; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg          
+:FMUL ST0, freg     is vexMode=0 & byte=0xD8; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg & ST0
 { 
     FPUInstructionPointer = inst_start;
     ST0 = ST0 f* freg; 
 }          
 
-:FMUL freg      is vexMode=0 & byte=0xDC; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg          
+:FMUL freg, ST0     is vexMode=0 & byte=0xDC; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg & ST0
 { 
     FPUInstructionPointer = inst_start;
     freg = freg f* ST0; 
 }         
 
-:FMULP freg     is vexMode=0 & byte=0xDE; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg          
+:FMULP freg, ST0    is vexMode=0 & byte=0xDE; frow=12 & fpage=1 & freg & ST0
 { 
     FPUInstructionPointer = inst_start;
     freg = ST0 f* freg; 
-- 
2.45.1

